Kind: ablation
Issue: #787
Takes out: thread_timeout()'s release whatever the timer's state -- it releases the fired timer's reference only when it finds the timer PENDING, as before #787. A wakeup that cancelled the timer while it was PENDING leaves the reference to nobody, and every one of timer_ref_test's sleepers, woken with its fired timer pending, ends the reaper with a count of 2 where the test's own is 1: never destroyed.
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 59 300 -smp 4
Expect: timer_ref_test: WRONG .* kept a reference after the reaper

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c
index 1bed2e92..4e65e15c 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c
@@ -536,9 +536,12 @@ thread_timeout(
 	if (thread->timer.set == TELT_PENDING) {
 		thread->timer.set = TELT_UNSET;
 		clear_wait_locked(thread, THREAD_TIMED_OUT, FALSE);
+		thread_unlock(thread);
+		thread_deallocate(thread);	/* 787-timeout-release-on-pending: only on PENDING, as before #787 */
+		splx(s);
+		return;
 	}
 	thread_unlock(thread);
-	thread_deallocate(thread);	/* the fired timer's reference */
 	splx(s);
 }
 
